        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "97bfae4a-b53b-5184-b12f-6fd1f519b90c",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Lowell George, Ian Hunter, Christopher Cross\n- Bands: Little Feat, Mott the Hoople\n- Songs: \"Ride Like the Wind\"\n\nFacts:\n- Lowell Thomas George was born on April 13, 1945, and he became an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer.\n- Ian Hunter Patterson was born on 3 June 1939, and he became a British singer-songwriter known as Ian Hunter.\n- Ian Hunter was the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople from the band's inception in 1969 until its dissolution in 1974.\n- Lowell George was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\n- Lowell George died on June 29, 1979.\n- Christopher Cross dedicated the song \"Ride Like the Wind\" to Lowell George on the album's inner sleeve after Lowell George had died in 1979.\n- Ian Hunter was also the lead singer for Mott the Hoople at the band's reunion performances in 2009 and 2013.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "5e0643a1-e910-5ba8-aab1-70905ccb35ab",
        "text": "Page: Lowell George. Sentence: Lowell Thomas George (April 13, 1945 – June 29, 1979) was an American songwriter, multi-instrumentalist, and record producer, who was the primary guitarist, vocalist, and songwriter for the rock band Little Feat.\nPage: Ian Hunter (singer). Sentence: Ian Hunter Patterson (born 3 June 1939), known as Ian Hunter, is a British singer-songwriter who is best known as the lead singer of the English rock band Mott the Hoople, from its inception in 1969 to its dissolution in 1974, and at the time of its 2009 and 2013 reunions.\nPage: Ride Like the Wind. Sentence: On the album's inner sleeve, Christopher Cross dedicated this song to Lowell George, formerly of the band Little Feat, who had died in 1979.",
